# NBA Playoff Companion — documentation-first (enforced)

**`docs/` is the long-term memory of this project.** Code must follow documented product vision. **Do not allow docs and code to drift apart.**

Read **`docs/WORKFLOW.md`** for the full contract.

---

## Before major work (mandatory)

Read **in order**:

1. `docs/APP_VISION.md`
2. `docs/DEVELOPMENT_PRIORITIES.md`
3. **Relevant feature doc:**

| Work area | Required doc |
|-----------|--------------|
| Live Game Center | `docs/LIVE_GAME_CENTER.md` — **source of truth** for safe mode, layers, refresh, reliability |
| Playoff bracket / status / elimination / offseason | `docs/PLAYOFF_ENGINE.md` — **source of truth** for advancement, elimination, bracket generation, offseason |
| Home, lineups, MI, tracker, history, previous rounds | `docs/PAGES.md` + area doc if exists |
| Legacy Tracker | `docs/LEGACY_TRACKER.md` |
| Team History | `docs/TEAM_HISTORY.md` |

**Major work** = new fan-visible behavior, engine rule change, live architecture change, or bracket/elimination logic change.

---

## After major work (mandatory)

Update **all that apply** in the **same session / commit** as code:

- `docs/COMPLETED_FEATURES.md` — shipped work
- `docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md` — new or resolved issues
- **Relevant feature doc** — if behavior or constants changed
- `docs/SYSTEMS_STATUS.md` — completion % or active priority / milestone
- `docs/DEVELOPMENT_PRIORITIES.md` — check off tasks; adjust P0/P1
- Bump **`Last updated: YYYY-MM-DD`** on every edited file

Sync `cursor-prompts/nba_app_*.md` mirrors when planning files are used.

---

## Feature requests & new features

- **Update docs first OR alongside code** in one change—never code-only for major features.
- Do not implement anything that conflicts with `docs/PAGES.md` or area docs without updating docs first.
- Move shipped items to `COMPLETED_FEATURES.md`; trim `ROADMAP.md` / priorities when done.

---

## Roadmap / planning conversations

When the user asks for **roadmap**, **feature plan**, **implementation plan**, **enhancement plan**, **project strategy**, or **future ideas**:

1. Read current `docs/` state (especially `DEVELOPMENT_PRIORITIES.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `SYSTEMS_STATUS.md`).
2. Update `docs/` (not only chat).
3. Keep `cursor-prompts/nba_app_*.md` sections: Current Priorities, Next Features, Long-Term Vision, Completed Features, Notes.
4. Long plans → `cursor-prompts/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-short-title.md`.

---

## Constants that must match docs

When changing these, update the matching doc section the same commit:

- `LIVE_GC_SAFE_MODE`, `PLAYOFF_BRACKET_REFRESH_MS`, Layer 1/2/3 behavior → `LIVE_GAME_CENTER.md`
- Series win (4 wins), `get_playoff_state_cached`, elimination, offseason → `PLAYOFF_ENGINE.md`

---

## Dev Lab

`product_docs.py` + Dev Lab **Product docs** tab parse `docs/`. After doc structure changes, verify the tab still shows: active priority, last updated, milestone, system completion %.

---

## Branch

Work on **`dev`** unless the user explicitly requests `main`.
